{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libexpat/libexpat/pulls/1272","id":3843712821,"node_id":"PR_kwDOBMl_Zc7lGmc1","html_url":"https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/pull/1272","diff_url":"https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/pull/1272.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/pull/1272.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libexpat/libexpat/issues/1272","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libexpat/libexpat/pulls/1272/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libexpat/libexpat/pulls/1272/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libexpat/libexpat/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libexpat/libexpat/issues/1272/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libexpat/libexpat/statuses/08baa7ef9d168b99094249998fd78f8d190526e5","number":1272,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[CVE-2026-56132] lib: `doProlog`: Fix out-of-bound scaffolding index store","user":{"login":"Smattr","id":203893,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzg5Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203893?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Smattr","html_url":"https://github.com/Smattr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Smattr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Smattr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Smattr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Smattr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Smattr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Smattr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Smattr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Smattr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Smattr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# Self-Diagnosis\r\n\r\n<!-- PLEASE ANSWER THE FOLLOWING: -->\r\n- [ ] This pull request fixes #ISSUE_NUMBER.\r\n- [x] This pull request is related to ANT-2026-00037\r\n- [ ] This pull request is small, uncontroversial, complete, and easy to review.\r\n- [x] I have enabled and run all GitHub Actions CI in my fork repository,\r\n  and hence expect CI to be all-green for this pull request.\r\n- [x] I have read the [contribution guidelines](https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/blob/HEAD/CONTRIBUTING.md), and this pull request meets these guidelines for contribution.\r\n- [ ] I had trouble understanding parts of this questionnaire. (Please elaborate.)\r\n\r\n\r\n# Description\r\n\r\nThis PR fixes an issue reported by Anthropic and Trail of Bits. Quoting Alessandro:\r\n\r\n> In doProlog() at xmlparse.c:5884 (HEAD on master at commit fc94fc36b8638b5f8311be5fdb216583b0ee8614), the write `dtd->scaffIndex[dtd->scaffLevel] = myindex;` runs past the end of the heap-allocated `dtd->scaffIndex` buffer.\r\n>\r\n> The root cause is at xmlparse.c:5862: the scaffold backing array is reallocated using the caller parser's per-parser `m_groupSize`, but the DTD struct (which carries scaffIndex) is shared between a parent parser and any external parameter-entity sub-parser created via `XML_ExternalEntityParserCreate(parent, NULL, ...)`. A sub-parser whose group nesting is shallower than the parent's can REALLOC the shared `scaffIndex` down to its own size; when the parent resumes and parses a deeper element content model, its bounds check passes (its private `m_groupSize` is still large enough), the doubling-grow path is skipped, and the next write lands past the shrunken buffer.\r\n\r\nCC @alessandrogario","labels":[{"id":527816086,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1Mjc4MTYwODY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libexpat/libexpat/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":null,"color":"ee0701","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":647724117,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw2NDc3MjQxMTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libexpat/libexpat/labels/security","name":"security","description"